      "description": "Effect 1 operates at the highest pressure and temperature, heated by live steam. Its vapour is hot enough to boil the liquor in effect 2, which runs at a lower pressure (lower boiling point), and so on to the last effect under vacuum. Each kilogram of steam evaporates roughly N × 0.8–1 kg of water in N effects (steam economy), at the cost of more heating surface.",
